<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59625" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρᾰνᾰός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, poet. word, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rocky, rugged</i>, in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always of Ithaca (exc. in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.445
			</span></i> where it is pr. n. of an island), <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.201
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.247
			</span></i>, al.; of Delos, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				1.3
			</span></i>; freq. of Athens, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>O.</u>
				7.82
			</span></i>, etc.: hence as pr. n., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κραναὰ
				πόλις</span> Athens, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				75
			</span></i>; simply 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ Κρανααί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Av.</u>
					123
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Κραναά</span> of the
			Acropolis, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				481
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κραναοί</span>
			<i>the people of Attica</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.44
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				9.1.18
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παῖδες Κραναοῦ</span> (Cranaos
			being a mythic king of Athens) <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				1011
			</span></i> (anap.) </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			generally, <i>hard</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χέλυς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					5.396
				</span></i>
			; of a fishing-rod, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥάβδος
			κ.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				4.364
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>stinging</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἀκαλῆφαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					560
				</span></i>
			. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρᾰνέα</span></b> , ἡ, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κράνεια</span>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
